{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "יהודה", :translit "yehudah", :gloss "Judah"} {:he "ביה", :translit "bah", :gloss "in it / with it"} {:he "ביה שמו", :translit "bah shemo", :gloss "in it is its name"} {:he "בראשית", :translit "bereshit", :gloss "in the beginning"} {:he "יהודה אתה יודוך", :translit "yehudah atah yodukha", :gloss "Judah, you, your brothers shall praise you"} {:he "הבאים אחריהם בים", :translit "haba'im acharayhem bayam", :gloss "those who come after them into the sea"} {:he "שמר לך", :translit "shamar lakh", :gloss "he kept for you"} {:he "מה טובו אהליך", :translit "mah tovu ohalekha", :gloss "how good are your tents"} {:he "ואעידה בם את השמים", :translit "ve'aidah bam et hashamayim", :gloss "and I will call heaven as witness against them"} {:he "כי ביה ה' צור עולמים", :translit "ki bah Hashem tzur olamim", :gloss "for in it the LORD is the rock of worlds"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :notarikon, :word "ביה", :expansion ["בראשית" "יהודה אתה יודוך" "הבאים אחריהם בים"]} {:kind :other, :note "שמר לך and מה טובו אהליך and ואעידה בם את השמים are additional expansions beyond the three-letter ביה, building toward a fuller acrostic"} {:kind :other, :note "Justification anchored in Isaiah 54:12: כי ביה ה' צור עולמים"}], :frame {:text "The letters of ביה in Isaiah 54:12 ('for in YH is the LORD, rock of worlds') are read as an allusion that God created the world with the letter bet, as in בראשית. Berakhot 55a records that the world was created with a bet. Genesis Rabbah 1:1 discusses the bet of בראשית specifically. The association of Judah with ביה reflects Deuteronomy 33:7 ('with his help against his enemies'), read alongside Genesis 49:8 where Judah is addressed.", :sources ["Isaiah 54:12" "Berakhot 55a" "Genesis Rabbah 1:1" "Deuteronomy 33:7" "Genesis 49:8"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אחיך ידך בעורף אויביך", :translit "akhekha yadekha be'oref oyvekha", :gloss "your brothers, your hand, on the neck of your enemies"} {:he "דוד", :translit "david", :gloss "David"} {:he "ואויבי תתה לי עורף", :translit "ve'oyvai titen li oref", :gloss "and my enemies you will give me [their] back of the neck"} {:he "ישתחוו לך", :translit "yishtachavu lakh", :gloss "they will bow down to you"} {:he "כל הארץ ישתחוו לך ויזמרו לך", :translit "kol ha'aretz yishtachavu lakh vezameru lakh", :gloss "all the earth will bow down to you and sing to you"} {:he "ואדונינו", :translit "ve'adoneinu", :gloss "and our lord"} {:he "ואדונינו מכל אלהים", :translit "ve'adoneinu mikol elohim", :gloss "and our lord above all gods"} {:he "ואדונינו דוד", :translit "ve'adoneinu david", :gloss "and our lord David"} {:he "כסאו כשמש נגדי", :translit "kis'o kashemesh negdi", :gloss "his throne as the sun before me"} {:he "די כרסון רמיו", :translit "dei karsun ramyey", :gloss "enough of the high throne"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אחיך ידך בעורף אויביך", :b "דוד"} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ישתחוו לך" "כל הארץ ישתחוו לך ויזמרו לך"]} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["ואדונינו מכל אלהים" "ואדונינו דוד"]}], :frame {:text "The verse 'your hand shall be on the neck of your enemies' (Genesis 49:8) applied to David, of whom Psalm 18:41 says 'you placed my enemies' neck [before me].' The dual-throne tradition appears in Hagigah 14a where it is taught that Metatron was given authority to sit and act as a deputy, prompting the objection 'there are indeed two powers in heaven.' The Aramaic phrase 'enough of the high throne' derives from Daniel 7:9–10, the throne-vision of the Ancient of Days. Psalm 89:37 promises David 'his throne shall be as the sun before Me.'", :sources ["Genesis 49:8" "Psalm 18:41" "Hagigah 14a" "Daniel 7:9" "Psalm 89:37"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :notarikon, :word "ביה", :expansion ["בראשית" "יהודה אתה יודוך" "הבאים אחריהם בים"], :initials ["ב" "י" "ה"], :by :selah, :initials-match? true} {:kind :other, :note "שמר לך and מה טובו אהליך and ואעידה בם את השמים are additional expansions beyond the three-letter ביה, building toward